      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(c)",
      "bbox": [
        245.0771026611328,
        288.98223876953125,
        254.4051055908203,
        296.3822326660156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fig. 15.",
      "bbox": [
        48.089698791503906,
        301.6661071777344,
        76.93624877929688,
        309.4070739746094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Convergence of the distribution of the path of latent states x1:T (note the change in vertical scale;",
      "bbox": [
        85.30570220947266,
        300.9798889160156,
        444.6502380371094,
        311.585693359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "initializing PMH sampling on a very unlikely initial path does not prevent the minimum mean-square error",
      "bbox": [
        48.08978271484375,
        310.6322326660156,
        443.6134033203125,
        318.3731994628906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "estimate of the latent states from converging; as few as 10 PMH iterations already begin to concentrate the",
      "bbox": [
        48.08978271484375,
        319.5983581542969,
        443.61517333984375,
        327.3393249511719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sampled paths around the true path (. . . . . . .), which is assumed here to be close to the mode of the pos-",
      "bbox": [
        48.08978271484375,
        326.2966003417969,
        443.6119079589844,
        336.3054504394531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "terior distribution thanks to the small observation noise, with very satisfactory results after 20000 iterations):",
      "bbox": [
        48.08978271484375,
        337.5306091308594,
        444.0260009765625,
        345.2715759277344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(a) initialized PMH state for x1:T (",
      "bbox": [
        48.08978271484375,
        345.8105163574219,
        172.0050506591797,
        356.4176025390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "); (b) average posterior mean path estimate for X1:T (",
      "bbox": [
        195.41729736328125,
        345.8118896484375,
        393.5164489746094,
        356.4176025390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "), PMH",
      "bbox": [
        416.9287109375,
        346.49810791015625,
        443.43035888671875,
        354.23907470703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Markov chain iteration i D10 and N D200 particles; (c) average posterior mean path estimate for X1:T , PMH",
      "bbox": [
        48.0902099609375,
        354.77801513671875,
        442.402587890625,
        365.3840026855469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Markov chain iteration i D20000 and N D200 particles",
      "bbox": [
        48.090057373046875,
        363.7444152832031,
        249.8235321044922,
        372.1716003417969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Adaption can be local (within ﬁlter) or global (sampled Markov chain history). Though currently",
      "bbox": [
        74.98880004882812,
        385.1601257324219,
        443.610107421875,
        393.47198486328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "particularly designed for approximate Bayesian computation methods, the work of Peters et al.",
      "bbox": [
        74.98880004882812,
        395.1226806640625,
        443.60205078125,
        403.4345397949219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(2010) incorporates into the mutation kernel of SMC samplers (Del Moral et al., 2006) the partial",
      "bbox": [
        74.98880004882812,
        405.0852355957031,
        443.6029357910156,
        413.3970947265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "rejection control (PRC) mechanism of Liu (2001), which is also beneﬁcial for PMCMC sampling.",
      "bbox": [
        74.9879150390625,
        415.04779052734375,
        443.6075134277344,
        423.3596496582031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "PRC adaption reduces degeneracy by rejecting a particle mutation when its incremental importance",
      "bbox": [
        74.9879150390625,
        425.0103454589844,
        443.60638427734375,
        433.32220458984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "weight is below a threshold cn. The PRC mutation kernel",
      "bbox": [
        74.9879150390625,
        434.9729309082031,
        290.3497009277344,
        443.2852783203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "qÅ",
      "bbox": [
        104.72101593017578,
